# examples/scenes/02_stretch, played at the size it opens in -- [window],
# 800x450 -- where every stretch draws the same court, so the HUD's line is
# what says which one is on. What the three look like in a window of another
# shape is the examples job's: tools/examples_build.sh boots this example in
# two more and reads the letterbox off the picture. See tests/e2e/script.h
# for the grammar.

# The .toml's mode, LETTERBOX.
10 shot letterbox

# M goes round: EXPAND. The gamepad's Y: NONE.
11 tap KEY_M
22 shot expand
23 tap GAMEPAD_BUTTON_RIGHT_FACE_UP
34 shot none

# And the button, for a screen with no keys: LETTERBOX again.
35 click 90 115
46 shot letterbox_by_the_button
46 expect scene CourtScene
46 end
